ually section 8 has \"Before 1.0.0\" etc. There's no other 0.9.x token. Let me check: `CL1-15` ... no. So only header and the specVersion row.\n\nWait \u2014 count.py scans current documents for `\\b[vV]?(0\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)\\b` and complains if != version. SPEC.md contains \"0.9.8\" only in the header and the specVersion example. Both change. Good.\n\nCHANGELOG.md: the newest heading at top must be `## 0.9.9 (candidate)`. Currently newest is `## 0.9.8 (candidate)`. We must not modify the existing 0.9.8 entry (it's history). But we need a new entry for 0.9.9 that claims no requirement changed. And test_06 checks `CADENCE_CONTRADICTION_RE` \u2014 no requirement id under **Breaking** in that entry. So the 0.9.9 entry must say \"no requirement changed\" in some phrasing.\n\nBut careful: the 0.9.8 entry below contains \"**Breaking** ... - CL1-10: ...\" but CADENCE_CONTRADICTION_RE only applies to `_changelog_entry(text, version)` which extracts text from the version heading to the next version heading. So the 0.9.9 entry's own text only.\n\nAlso count.py scans \"current documents\": `current = [p for p in md if \"record\" not in p.relative_to(ROOT).parts[:1] and p.name != \"CHANGELOG.md\"]`. So CHANGELOG.md is exempt from version token scanning. Good.\n\nBut wait \u2014 test_09 `measure_documents_clean` scans CURRENT_DOCUMENTS = README, CONTRIBUTING, DRAFT-NOTE, GOVERNANCE, SECURITY, NOTICE, PATENTS, SPEC + examples. CHANGELOG not included. Good.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md: test_07 requires the gap sentence to keep naming which release shipped without a record (0.9.8 or \"the previous release\" in words) and where the note is, and it must carry no version token count.py reads as stale. Since the release is now 0.9.9, the token `0.9.8` in CONTRIBUTING.md is a stale token (count.py reads current documents; CONTRIBUTING.md's tokens must equal 0.9.9). So the sentence must be rewritten to name the release in words: \"The release before this one shipped without a record \u2014 the gap note in `record/` says why\". And test_07's check (c): claim found, named release found (\"the release before this one\"), own_note absent, names_this_release False \u2192 no problem. Good.\n\nAlso test_07 checks the base sentences survive, with version tokens masked. It compares the base CONTRIBUTING sentences to current ones. The base sentence containing the fact is exempt. Other sentences must survive with version tokens masked. So we must change only the fact-carrying sentence.\n\nLet me look at the base CONTRIBUTING.md text (which is the current one in the chat):\n\n```\nA behavioral change to the checker, the fixtures or the schema is itself a job: the bar is frozen before the\nchange, a reader who could not see the maker's answer reads it, and the release carrying it ships a record.\nVersion 0.9.8 shipped without one \u2014 `record/RECORD-GAP-v0.9.8.md` says why \u2014 and `count.py` now refuses a\nrelease that neither carries a record nor declares its absence.\n```\n\nThe fact sentence: \"Version 0.9.8 shipped without one \u2014 `record/RECORD-GAP-v0.9.8.md` says why \u2014 and `count.py` now refuses a release that neither carries a record nor declares its absence.\"\n\nWait, sentences(text) joins lines. The paragraph is one unit (lines joined). So the whole paragraph may be one \"sentence\" unit for carries_version_fact. Hmm, sentences() flushes on blank lines and paragraphs. So the entire paragraph \"A behavioral change ... absence.\" is ONE unit. carries_version_fact matches if it has \"shipped without\" and a release name and \"`record/`\" or RECORD-GAP. Yes.\n\nNow test_07's (d) arm: for each base unit not carrying the fact, if its masked version appears in now_units, fine. The paragraph carries the fact, so it's exempt.\n\nNow (a): survivors \u2014 any token in CONTRIBUTING.md != 0.9.9. After rewriting, tokens: none (we remove both 0.9.8 tokens). But careful: masked comparison in (d) for other units. Also `TCC BY` nothing.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 after th